CAUTION: External Email

Hello Michal,



Below you will find the details of the possibility of direct API connection=
 of your system with DHL Express. If you need further information, please f=
eel free to contact me via email or we can schedule a meeting through Teams=
.



*       API Protocol: JSON / RESTv2
*       API Guide: DHL Express API<https://url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/r=
AxmCG6xjxhNKE8JQfKfmXhBoEDV?domain=3Ddeveloper.dhl.com> (registration not r=
equired)
*       API can be customized according to your requirements: For any speci=
fic functions or services, please contact me.
*       Attachments: An Excel file with API requests and examples for shipm=
ents within and outside the EU includes information for shipment creation, =
rate retrieval, and shipment tracking services.



The API response will include:

a.      Shipment number (waybill)
b.      Label in format (PDF, ZPL) in base64 encoding
c.      Tracking URL for API
d.      Other requested information





To connect to the API, you need a DHL Express account, endpoint, and API cr=
edentials. Please send us the following information so we can generate and =
send the API credentials to your email.



Required information to generate API credentials:

Customer DHL Express Accounts:

Customer Contact Name:

Customer Email:

Customer Telephone:

Customer Address Line:

Customer City:

Customer Postcode:









QR Code

Information about generating a QR code can be found below. An example API r=
equest for this shipment type is provided below and can also be found in th=
e Excel file under the "Create Shipment =96 Label Free" tab.



Below I describe these changes in more detail. I have also attached an exam=
ple showing how the shipment QR code looks.

Please note: The Label Free service is subject to several requirements and =
limitations, which are described below.



Label Free Service Activation

   *    The Label Free service must first be enabled on your API account.
   *    If you decide to use this service, please let me know and I will en=
able it on your API credentials. We will first activate it in the test envi=
ronment and, once everything has been successfully tested, we will enable i=
t in the production environment as well.



   Supported Destinations

   *    As with the PLT service (electronic Invoice), there are countries t=
hat do not support the Label Free service.
   *    If Label Free data is sent through the API for a destination that d=
oes not support this service, the API will return an error and the shipment=
 label will not be generated.
   *    Please find attached a list of destinations that support the Label =
Free service.



   Non-EU Shipments

   *    For Non-EU shipments, the PLT service (WY) / Electronic Invoice mus=
t always be used together with the Label Free service. Otherwise, the Label=
 Free service cannot be used.
   *    If a country does not support PLT, it also does not support the Lab=
el Free service.



   DHL Service Point Support

*       Customers can verify which DHL Service Points accept Label Free shi=
pments with a QR code by using the DHL Service Point Locator: DHL Service P=
oint Locator<https://url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/Ic0nCJ6AmAhW3ln8DIGh34h=
y1nR1?domain=3Dlocator.dhl.com>



API DATA

QR Code Generation

*       To have the API return a QR code in addition to the shipment label,=
 the following data must be included in the API request.
*       The QR code is returned in the same manner as the shipment label, e=
ncoded in Base64, but it is always provided in PNG format.



API Request

"outputImageProperties": {

  "encodingFormat": "pdf",

  "imageOptions": [

    {

      "isRequested": true,

      "typeCode": "qr-code"

    }

  ]

}



Field description:

*       encodingFormat: Defines the format of generated documents, such as =
commercial invoices (if applicable).
*       isRequested: Indicates whether the QR code should be generated and =
returned in the API response.
*       typeCode =3D "qr-code": Requests generation of a QR code, which is =
always returned as a PNG image.



Additional Value-Added Services

*       In addition, the following value-added services must be included in=
 the API request:

*       PZ =96 Label Free service
*       PT =96 Data Staging 03 service

*       The Data Staging service ensures that shipment data is retained wit=
hin DHL Express systems for three months.



API Request

"valueAddedServices": [

  {

    "serviceCode": "PZ"

  },

  {

    "serviceCode": "PT"

  }

]



 Field description:

*       serviceCode =3D "PZ": Enables the Label Free service.
*       serviceCode =3D "PT": Enables the Data Staging 03 service, which st=
ores shipment data in DHL Express systems for three months.





Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.

Thank you for your cooperation, and have a nice day.



